CORE
Test
--function Test.main --verbosity 10 -cp target/classes
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^identified invokedynamic at java::Test.main:\(\)V address 0 for lambda: java::Test.lambda\$main\$0:\(I\)I
^identified invokedynamic at java::Test.main:\(\)V address 6 for lambda: java::Test.lambda\$main\$1:\(I\)I
--
^ignoring invokedynamic
--
This exercises two cases that aren't currently supported: stub interfaces and stub superinterfaces.
All we require at this point is that jbmc shouldn't crash when these are seen.
With JDK 11+ bytecode, JBMC now handles these lambdas rather than ignoring them.
